5-b162-3574ee933cd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424971 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then the phrase \"nine more than a number\" can be written as\n\n$$\nx+9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424972 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424972 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108488" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424972 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424972 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Twenty-five more than a number.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424972 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45774186-e405-50e3-9083-00b3a8647ac3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424972 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $a$, then the phrase \"twenty-five more than a number\" can be written as\n\n$$\na+25.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424973 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424973 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184139" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424973 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424973 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Twenty-five fewer than a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $n$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424973 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49b8ccfc-8c8f-513c-976c-7189fb53e754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424973 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $n,$ then the phrase \"twenty-five fewer than a number\" can be written as \n\n$$\nn-25.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424974 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424974 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424974 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424974 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a variable?\n\nI. $3$\n\nII. $1-x$\n\nIII. $y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424974 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4bbee0aa-5b29-5213