th's house. If the distance from Beth's house to school is $d$ miles, then the distance from Carl's house to school is{{field-1}}miles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424977 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a26167a2-2a64-57a1-8bc2-6bd8a04d1786" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424977 #edb/ref 1074 "We know the distance from Beth's house to school is $d$ miles, and the distance from Carl's house to school is $9$ miles less than that from Beth's house. Therefore, the distance from Carl's house to school is $d-9$ miles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108356" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424978 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424978 #edb/ref 1071 "How many distinct variables are there in the algebraic expression $y+2w+z-2wx+5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b81b7456-a2b2-5074-8d35-61b208d56683" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424978 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression contains a total of four variables, $w,x,y,$ and $z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424979 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424979 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424979 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424979 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"One more than a number.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424979 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f08382ab-8492-5563-871a-83c2011eac57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424979 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $a$, then the phrase \"one more than a number\" can be written as\n\n$$\na+1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424980 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424980 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424980 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424980 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"$35$ less than a number.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424980 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5c73352-21c9-5c19-bb4b-0d12d53e07e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424980 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $q$, then the phrase can be written as\n\n$$\nq-35.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424981 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424981 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424981 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Fifteen more than a number.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f967a99f-911e-59b2-80e7-a5ba0f5de422" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424981 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then the phrase \"fifteen more than a number\" can be written as\n\n$$\nx+15\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424982 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424982 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424982 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424982 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a variable?\n\nI. $b$\n\nII. $b+c$\n\nIII. $c$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424982 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fab7b2b9-4fb5-56fc-9278-9df96447599b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424982 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's look at each one in turn.\n\nI. $b$ is a variable because it's a single letter by itself.\n\nII. $b+c$ is an algebraic expression, not a variable.\n\nIII. $c$ is a variable because it's a single letter by itself.\n\nSo, only choices I and III represent a variable." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
